      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8934",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ \u22ee & \u22ee & \u22f1 & \u22ee \\\\ 0 & 0 & \u22ef & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/example-8934.json",
          "file_sha256": "da02ce27aaa2c9a46df017a0f57aa8d0409316a40830a84829049a13ac70bbf5"
